---
// privacy.astro — Archex Ecosystem Privacy Policy
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — Archex"
  description="Archex Ecosystem Privacy Policy. Explaining our data handling practices, purpose-specific consent, and privacy rights across archexweb.in."
  canonical="https://www.archexweb.in/privacy/"
  activePath="/privacy"
>
  <div class="shell legal-container">
    <div class="legal-header">
      <span class="tech-tag">Legal & Data Governance</span>
      <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy Policy<span class="hl-dot">.</span></h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">
        <span>Effective Date: November 2026</span>
        <span class="meta-sep">•</span>
        <span>Applies to: archexweb.in and related parent brand properties</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Indian Legal Review Advisory Callout -->
    <div class="legal-advisory" role="note">
      <div class="advisory-icon" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
          <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
          <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
          <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="advisory-text">
        <strong>Legal Notice & Indian Regulatory Context:</strong>
        This Privacy Policy outlines data handling practices across Archex. While drafted to uphold core data protection principles under the Information Technology Act, 2000 and the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (India), formal operational policies and future statutory rules (as phased commencement notifications take effect) remain subject to confirmation and review by a qualified Indian legal practitioner.
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>1. Operator Identity, Brand Architecture & Business Structure</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Archex</strong> is an independently operated brand managed by <strong>Kaif</strong>, an individual based in West Bengal, India.
        </p>
        <p>
          Archex is not a separately incorporated company or limited liability partnership. References to "Archex", "we", "us" and "our" refer to the individual operating the brand, unless the context indicates otherwise.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Archex ecosystem operates through three distinct disciplines:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Archex Craft</strong> (craft.archexweb.in) — Software engineering, digital product development, and technical systems. Also serves as the centralised contact and enquiry destination.</li>
          <li><strong>Archex Studio</strong> (studio.archexweb.in) — Brand identity, creative direction, UI/UX, and digital experiences.</li>
          <li><strong>Archex GTM</strong> (gtm.archexweb.in) — Go-to-market strategy, positioning, and growth execution (currently under development).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          All three practices operate under the same individual founder and are not independent incorporated businesses. This parent website (archexweb.in) serves an informational and gateway purpose.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>2. Interaction Stages & Data Processing Scope</h2>
        <p>
          To maintain transparency, we distinguish between three distinct stages of interaction with Archex:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Stage 1 — Visiting this Parent Website (archexweb.in):</strong> This website is purely informational. It does not host interactive contact forms, project submission forms, lead qualification forms, or newsletter opt-in checkboxes. We do not collect names, work emails, or project briefs on this parent domain.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Stage 2 — Voluntarily Submitting an Enquiry via Archex Craft (craft.archexweb.in):</strong> When you choose to submit an enquiry or project brief, you navigate to our centralised portal at <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in/contact">craft.archexweb.in/contact</a>. Data submitted there is collected directly into Archex Craft's managed infrastructure and is governed by the <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in/privacy">Archex Craft Privacy Policy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Stage 3 — Communicating During a Commercial Engagement:</strong> If a discussion progresses into a professional services engagement, information exchange is governed by a separate written proposal, Statement of Work (SOW), or commercial agreement entered into with the operator.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>3. Technical & Infrastructure Data (Parent Website)</h2>
        <p>
          While archexweb.in collects no user-submitted form data, the website operates over the public internet. Like virtually all web properties, our hosting and edge content delivery network (CDN) automatically process limited technical request information:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access & Server Logs:</strong> Standard server logs capturing IP addresses, request timestamps, HTTP request methods, referring URLs, and requested resources.</li>
          <li><strong>Browser & Device Metadata:</strong> User-agent strings, browser type, and operating system attributes necessary to return properly rendered HTML, CSS, and web fonts.</li>
          <li><strong>Security & Diagnostics:</strong> Telemetry processed by edge infrastructure solely for threat detection, rate limiting, and DDoS mitigation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This technical data is processed strictly for the operational integrity, performance, and security of the website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>4. Cookies & Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Archex Web does not deploy third-party advertising cookies, behavioural profiling trackers, cross-site pixels, or remarketing scripts on this parent website.
        </p>
        <p>
          Any client-side browser storage utilized is strictly limited to essential functional operations, such as asset caching and responsive navigation state.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>5. Centralised Enquiries & Internal Data Handling</h2>
        <p>
          All contact inquiries across the ecosystem are centralised through Archex Craft:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Official Contact Destination:</strong> <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in/contact">https://craft.archexweb.in/contact</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          Enquiries submitted through Craft are reviewed by the individual operator (Kaif). Information is not automatically broadcast or shared across separate practice workflows unless an enquiry explicitly pertains to or requests services involving creative direction (Studio) or go-to-market strategy (GTM).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>6. Data Retention & Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Because archexweb.in does not collect or maintain a local database of personal records or customer briefs, no personal client records are retained on this parent domain.
        </p>
        <p>
          Technical access logs processed by hosting and edge network providers are maintained on transient, rolling retention schedules (typically 14 to 30 days) solely for security forensics, traffic hygiene, and diagnostic purposes, after which they are routinely aggregated or purged.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>7. Security Measures</h2>
        <p>
          All web traffic to archexweb.in is enforced over HTTPS using modern TLS encryption. We maintain strict administrative security controls and utilize established edge hosting infrastructure with automated threat mitigation to protect our web presence against unauthorized access or tampering.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>8. Your Privacy Rights & Contact Handling</h2>
        <p>
          Under applicable Indian data protection law—including the Information Technology Act, 2000 (and applicable rules) and the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (as statutory provisions and rules are notified)—individuals possess rights regarding personal data held by data fiduciaries. These include the rights to request access, correction, erasure, and grievance redressal.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Submitting Privacy &amp; Grievance Requests:</strong> You may submit privacy requests, data access inquiries, consent withdrawals, or privacy-related complaints through our official email channels or via our centralised online contact desk:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Privacy &amp; Data Protection:</strong> <a href="mailto:privacy@archexweb.in">privacy@archexweb.in</a></li>
          <li><strong>Grievance Redressal:</strong> <a href="mailto:grievance@archexweb.in">grievance@archexweb.in</a></li>
          <li><strong>General Communications:</strong> <a href="mailto:hello@archexweb.in">hello@archexweb.in</a></li>
          <li><strong>Central Web Intake:</strong> <a href="https://craft.archexweb.in/contact">craft.archexweb.in/contact</a> (select "Data Protection / Privacy Request")</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Privacy requests and grievances are handled directly by <strong>Kaif</strong> as the individual responsible for data protection across Archex. We do not claim to operate a corporate Data Protection Officer. We evaluate and respond to all legitimate requests in accordance with statutory timelines under applicable Indian law.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-container {
    padding-top: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px);
    padding-bottom: clamp(60px, 9vw, 110px);
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 32px;
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin-top: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .hl-dot {
    color: var(--signal);
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .meta-sep {
    color: var(--line);
  }

  /* Advisory Callout */
  .legal-advisory {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 16px 20px;
    background-color: #ffffff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--signal);
    border-radius: 3px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .advisory-icon {
    color: var(--signal);
    margin-top: 2px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .advisory-text {
    font-size: 13.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 36px;
  }

  .legal-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 14px;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 19px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    padding-bottom: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
  }

  .legal-section p {
    font-size: 15.5px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: 20px;
    position: relative;
  }

  .legal-section li::before {
    content: '—';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--signal);
    font-family: var(--mono);
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: var(--signal);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>

